This is my first ascension post. There are many like it, but this one is
mine. 

Thanks Janis!

Since this is my first one I hope I get this right. I don't think I'll be
able to give as good a summary as I would like, but here goes.
Go easy on the spelling, a very excited non native english speaker typed
this up.
[Ed. It's gotten a overly long, keep in mind that I had done the quest or
never been below Sokoban before this run. So everything was rather new to
me ;)]

Here we go:

This game started out OK, random generated char was a valk. Great, I like
valks. 
After char generation she was off to a lousy start. Went to mine town, no
BoH, went down all the way to medusa no BoH did sokoban, got a "oR. Above
the medusa level maybe three shops ( two general, one booze) no BoH. Went
downto mines end, to find out it was not the end I was used to. I have seen
two different ends before, in this one I was unable to find a luckstone or
even a wine cellar.

By now I did collect quite a number of spellbooks, (it's a shame it doesn't
list the spells I knew at asension) so I decided she would grow up to be a
spellcaster. I learned some spells, locked away some spellbooks in a chest
I dragged to sokoban (the only level I could reliably find at a reasonable
depth.). 
After that I went around all levels up to medusa once more to see where the
rng had hidden the BoH, but couldn't find it. I did however find a /oW and
got wished for one along with armour scrolls of charging and magic marker.
By this time I was worried about the lack of water, I have had maybe 4
bottles the whole game and making some at fountains. So I ran around some
more as I really wanted some holy water along for the trip, I never found
any.

After that I noticed I was at about level 25 and felt pretty good about
myself, and decided to go on the quest. From there on I have had nothing
but good luck. Apart from this one time I think it might have been before
the trip I got amnesia of one of those damned mind flayers, I saw no use
for genocide, but that conviced me otherwise and wiped them out right then
and there.

After the quest I pretty much sailed through the levels below death without
any problems (Is this always so easy). To be honest I got pretty bored with
the mazes down there, killed Vlad, the rich dude in te castle, had an
argument with Juiblex who swallowed me (Nothing a zap with a wand of death
and a couple of whacks with a silver sable couldn't fix).
I thought the middle of the game was ridiculously easy.

After that went up te relearn my spells, decided to drag the spellbooks
along because I had no idea how long, or deep the dungeons would go on. 

Did the invocation thing, had a problem with the Wizard(s) which prompted me
to post to (and read) r.g.r.n, got a nice tip whacked the wizards over the
head with a chickatrice.

Went back up, my trusted Mjollnir won a few short arguments with the wizard
on the way up after I learned the coward fled up the stairs when
threatened.

On level 1, saved my game spent some worrying about my lack of healing
potions (about 5 extra, one full) and holy water (none), decided to give it
a shot because I didn't know where to get any and I had (5 eucalyptus
leaves, a few uni-horns and knew the extra healing spell).

So next were the planes.

EARTH:
Peer into Orb of Fate, great teleport only two zaps with a /oD away.
Met only a few elementals on the way no problem.

Next up AIR (I think):
Oops forgot my pet Angel, lets go back. After putting on boots of levitation
(I really should wish for a ring next time).
Went back, got my angel, Peered into the OoF evaded most of the baddies
clobbered mayba 4 or five with Mjollnir and was at the next portal.

FIRE:
Again went back to fetch my pet, kept my Levitation boots on.
Got boxed in by fire elementals, remembered I had a =oC put it on killed a
few lizards, lost a potion of healing to fire damage, put the rest back in
the bag (Hoping I would have enough time to get it when I need it). and on
to the next.

WATER:
Boring, go back fetch my pet, peer into OoF finally got to the place I need
to be, clubbered a number of E's along the way never braeking a sweat.
Portal gone, I thought as everything seems to be moving about in air bubles
maybe the portal does aswell.. 
Swam around some more, can't find the danmn portal and somewhere out of the
blue swam into it....

ASTRAL PLANE:
PANIC, surrounded by three angels, take abreat check them out... Angels of
Tyr. Pfew, I'm OK. So I go back and fetch my pet, step aside... Look
back... no portal. 
Bummer, I was getting attached to my pet. Anyway, no use being sentimental
about it, lots of high numbers on the radar, su I decide to peer into the
OoF to find the altar I need to be.
ZAP! I get blasted by the stupid thing, I'm hallucinating, I apply a
uni-horn, nothing... Try again, nothing. ( I figured the stupid things
don't work on this plane). 
I decide to wait it out as there were onle the three Angels nearby, I Put on
blindfold to map out some of the level,.. gulp that's alot of whatevers.
Wait some more, get zapped by something, figure its one of the A's take of
my =oC.
Wait some more hear a door open,.. see a lot of somethings coming towards
me, decide to take my chances with the A's put the =oC on.

Hallucination wore off, saw three demons, Checked them out.. Death,
Pestilence and Famine, nice...

Had no clue so I decided to check out Pestilence first,... BAD MOVE!!
Pestilence infected my a dozen of times, wasted all my potions of healing,
eucalyptus leaves and the stupid amulet made casting extra healing a
problem. I tried hitting him, zapping him with extra healing thinking that
might be a good idea even though I could use the spells myself (all to no
effect). 
So I ran away from him as fast I could, (not very fast being confused and
stunned after each hit from him.) finally manged to get some creatures
between him and me, cast charm monster, no luck...
Ran away smoe more after deperately applying the unicorn horn again (so they
do work) ran into Death killed him without major incident. Went up to an
altar, was made aware of a priest of Odin, figured I needed to go to
another altar. Ran into Pestilence again and figured I would die then and
there, got out a "oLS put it on and prepared for the worst. 
Then I found my new friend Death again, maneuvered him between me and
Pestilence and and the three of os moved around the level for some time.
Got to the rightmost altar Checked it out, it's the altar of.... Odin! 
OK, now I get it the stupid priests are jumbled all over the place, nice... 

Fighting my way back to the central altar, zapped myself with enlightenment
found out I couldn't pray... Checked my supplies, only one eucalyptus leaf
left... And I had to pass Pestilence maneuvered to the opposite side of one
a round chamber, and figured I would get hit by him once if I don't get
blocked, sure enough he shows up. I throw Mjolnir at him as often as I
could,run a circle around him get infected, keep running, get blocked by a
stubborn A. Eat my last leaf whack at the angel get blocked again, by a
number of A's blocking a door. Throw MJ at Pestilence a few more times only
to have him corned me in the doorway....

Knowing I'm dead, I check my inventory... no more potions, leaves, and all
out of spellpoints. No time to switch my robe for [coD.
Had put on "oLS somewhere along the way and hoped it wouldn't curse or take
away my inventory like in a bones pile, hoped it would save me from death
by pestilence...
So I give Pestilence a few more futile whacks as I have ran out of options.
And after the second whack... He actually drops dead!!!
I couldn't believe my eyes, checked my stats inventorya again. I'm only 15
steps away from the second (center) altar.


After saving the game, making some coffee. I remove Life Saving put my
Conflict back on, whack a few Angels, get to the altar room, check the
altar and sure enough it's Tyr.
In the room is only the priest and a Xorn, I notice the Xorn whacking the
priest, I quickly check my stats, put on a blindfold to double check for
any riders. And kill the Xorn, drag is heavy ass onto the altar to
sacrifice it. 
Standing on the altar I decide against it and decide to offer the amulet
first like the paranoid coward I am, afraid it might screw up my game at
the last minute. 

So there I was:

